  "goodToKnow": "Die Volksrepublik is a people's republic, the name used by communist states: die Volksrepublik China, and until 1989 Poland, Hungary and Bulgaria. The GDR called itself Deutsche Demokratische Republik instead. China has been one of Germany's largest trading partners for years, a relationship now debated under the term De-Risking. Das Volk means people or nation. Plural: die Volksrepubliken."
